      "where": "verbs.tenses / verbs.sequence",
      "detail": "The sorting rule between these two subtopics turns on whether a subordinate clause is governed by a past verb of saying, thinking, knowing or perceiving, and it names only said, realised, discovered, noticed, found. It does not say whether decision or intention verbs (decided, chose, agreed, planned) count. Q22 (We had been living in this neighborhood for ten years before we decided to move) is fixed by both a time expression and a linked past verb, decided, that is not on the named list, so a classifier without the paper's own answer key would genuinely split between the two subtopics."
